                  },
                  "linkStyle": {
                    "inherit": true,
                    "linkColor": "#514293",
                    "linkHoverColor": "#514293",
                    "linkUnderline": true,
                    "linkHoverUnderline": true
                  },
                  "text": "I grew up with a round metal spice tin in the kitchen. The lid slid open, and inside were small bowls of cumin, turmeric, coriander, chilli, salt and pepper. A pinch here. A pinch there. Dinner begins.<br><br>Years later, I learned that some of those pairings help each other work, like black pepper with turmeric. That tin had been doing clever things all along. Rituals that taste good tend to last.",
                  "fontSize": "13px",
                  "fontFamily": {
                    "label": "Helvetica",
                    "value": "helvetica,sans-serif"
                  },
                  "color": "#1A1A1A",
                  "textAlign": "left",
                  "lineHeight": "160%",
                  "containerPadding": "4px 32px 16px"
                }
